[repo-allocation name=cx-repos
  [doc [#
THE REPO ALLOCATION — every tracked path in this tree, assigned to the
repository it moves to under the approved multi-repo shape (#1589, the owner
approved the shape 2026-09-21; the execution tracker is #1591). This file is
the allocation as DATA; scripts/repos_allocation_gate.cx is the check that
every tracked file lands in exactly one repo and that no rule here is dead.
It is what each extraction's history filter consumes, and it is the #1077
lesson — enumerate every artifact dimension before anything moves — made
executable.

Nothing here carries a `RULED:` id yet: the decision page superseding
cx_partition.md §5/§5.1 is item 5 on #1591. Until it lands this file states
the plan, and the gate keeps the plan total over the tree.

TWO KINDS OF ROW.
  [repo name= group= ring= ships= about= status=? at=? pins=? vmodule=? why=?]
      one row per destination repository. `group` is the front-page group
      (core | platform | binding | ecosystem | dist), `ring` is 0, 1 or none,
      `ships` is how the repo reaches a user (binary | package | pypi | crate |
      go-module | v-module | editor | none | archived).
      `status=extracted` says the extraction is DONE (RULED: RS-12): the
      repository exists, it owns its paths, and none of them is tracked here
      any more -- so the row carries no `[path]` rules, `at=` records the sha
      `cx` pins it at in deps.cxd, and the gate exempts it from the empty-repo
      refusal while adding the converse one (a `status=extracted` repo that is
      still the first match for a tracked file is an extraction stopped half
      way). Absent `status` means the plan is still a plan.
      `pins='<repo> ...'` and `vmodule=<m>` are the V products' import
      graph (RULED: RS-24, owner D28a): `pins` is the Pins column of the
      #1589 table -- the repositories this one builds on, acyclic -- and
      `vmodule` names the V module the repository compiles from `vcx/<m>/`
      (D31a: flat). A product row gains `vmodule` in the commit that splits
      it. xap's split made xap `vcx/xap/` (`module xap`, the composer with
      it); fabric's split, the last, emptied `vcx/platform/` (`module platform`,
      the RESIDUE the not-yet-split products shared) and xap's PHASE B retired
      it with its catch-all rule. scripts/product_import_gate.cx holds every import under a
      vmodule directory to these pins; the rings (the `core` rows) are always
      importable.
  [path prefix= repo=]  /  [path exact= repo=]
      one allocation rule. A tracked file belongs to the FIRST rule, in
      document order, whose `exact` equals the path or whose `prefix` is a
      leading substring of it. Specific rules are therefore written ABOVE
      general ones; the gate refuses a rule that matches no file, which is how
      a shadowed or stale rule is caught.

HOW TO READ A DECISION HERE. Where a module's repo is not the obvious one,
the rule carries a `why=`. The recurring reasons, once:
  - split by PRODUCT, not by dependency graph (owner, 2026-09-21);
  - the ring membership test (cx_partition.md §10): a module that imports
    nothing and opens no socket is Ring 1 and lives with the language —
    did, vc, authz, bus, the xsp frame codec, iowatch;
  - a shared codec stays in the language repo: saml/scim/oidc/soap/graphql/
    ws/email/http-client have callers outside the one product;
  - a module whose only consumer is one product moves to that product:
    ft → store, sasl → mail, diagram → tooling;
  - the store owns engine, streams (journal/live/audit) AND server, as
    Postgres does; the session module sits above it in identity;
  - `scripts/`, `tools/`, `docs*/`, `bench/`, `examples/`, `_gate_evidence/`
    and the root files are the build, release, site and evidence machinery of
    the whole — they go to `cx`, the distribution repo, and are re-homed per
    repo as each extraction lands (a repo takes its own gates with it).
#]]

  [; ── the destinations ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
  [repo name=cx group=dist ring=none ships=binary about='the front door: pins every repo, builds the four cx builds and libcx-core/libcx, holds the site, the release, the installer']
  [repo name=cx-core-data group=core ring=0 ships=binary status=extracted at=2ddcf938395e812d93b229b63c925334b0d4d5ab about='the data format: reader, writer, canonical form, schema, codecs, libcx-core, the data-only cx' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-7, RS-12, D68a), the first V repository: deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork, its V modules (cx, cli, fixtures, arrow, cmd_data, the re2 shim, and since D56a grading -- the corpus grading cores and the cx corpus body both profiles run) are compiled from deps/cx-core-data/vcx through -path, and its data-language corpus and fixtures are graded from the pin. It owns no tracked path here any more: the 87 allotted files this tree grades, builds or documents are re-allocated by D68a to cx and cx-core-code in the block below, each with its reason, and their copies left the repository at the sha at= records']
  [repo name=cx-core-code group=core ring=1 ships=binary about='the language: evaluator, stdlib, LSP, libcx, the cli and embed builds']
  [repo name=cx-platform-net group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxnet status=extracted at=0a4f2114af1e29a19362b24069061c913c9a0374 pins='cx-core-code' about='sockets, TLS, the HTTP server, the XSP transport bindings, ftp, sftp, file_surface' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-24, #1591 item 20), the third V product (after core-data): its own vcx/cxnet/ (module cxnet) and vcx/transport/ leave with it. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s http, net, ftp and sftp rows -- plus the file_surface catalog row -- name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-platform-mail group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=mail status=extracted at=d0d27c1d11cd8ca70b6f94f8fa86b5a83d1634e0 pins='cx-platform-net' about='SMTP and IMAP, server and client cores, sasl' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-19, D71a, D76c; #1591 item 20): its V module vcx/mail/ (module mail) compiles from deps/cx-platform-mail/vcx through -path and its spec, corpus and source are graded from the pin. The four files that stayed until D71a -- the declared pure halves of imap and smtp, once called INTRA-MODULE by vcx/code/stdlib_dispatch.v -- left with the builtin-dispatch registration hook: code exposes register_stdlib_builtin and mail\'s own init() registers smtp and imap. sasl\'s V dispatch, vcx/code/stdlib_sasl.v, is the core\'s (D76c: Ring 1 and pure), while its spec, corpus and source stay here. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s sasl, imap and smtp rows name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-platform-identity group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=identity pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-net' at=4cfa0234d63bf86dacbbafe53f7dab29e9bd4add about='sessions, the XSP-AUTH handshake, did:web, authz-store, vc-revocation' why='PARTLY EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3): deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork -- NOT YET PUSHED to cx-home/cx-platform-identity (component-repo pushes are the integrator\'s, RS-8; the commit is prepared in the mover\'s clone and named by sha in RESULTS.md, per the K3 brief) -- its V module (vcx/identity/, module identity) compiles from deps/cx-platform-identity/vcx through -path, and its session/authz-store/did-web/vc-revocation/xsp-auth spec/corpus/source are graded from the pin. One file remains below: xsp-auth\'s declared Ring-1 half (modules.cxd half=), vcx/code/stdlib_xsp_auth.v -- a permanent architecture split (RS-24/D34a: the store server runs it and the store V module may not import identity), not a discovered same-module wall awaiting a hook, so it is named here and in K3\'s RESULTS.md, not a LETTER. The row takes status=extracted the day it is pushed']
  [repo name=cx-platform-store group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=store pins='cx-core-code cx-platform-net' at=36bdd0fb08ac793fde1a567a62e1e518d010c1c9 about='the storage engine, its substrates, journal/live/audit, ft, and the store server' why='PARTLY EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, D71a, D73a; #1591 item K3): the RS-24 vcx/store/ split (module store) already stood alone from vcx/platform/, so extraction moved it, vcx/cxstore/ and vcx/cmd/store_ whole out -- store\'s, journal\'s, live\'s and audit\'s spec, corpus and source now name deps/cx-platform-store/ in registry/modules.cxd, and so does ft\'s CX-level surface (stdlib/ft.cx, its spec, its corpus), even though ft is a Ring-1 cx-stdlib module the store repository merely carries as its only consumer. One file remains: vcx/code/stdlib_ft.v, ft\'s V dispatch half -- code\'s stdlib_dispatch.v names ft_stdlib_builtin() and both of eval.v\'s env chains name ft_stdlib_builtin_env(); the D71a hook carries the env-free half as is, the env half needs the hook\'s env-aware twin first (a follow-up branch, named in _gate_evidence/pipeline_dispatch/RESULTS.md). The three vcx/cmd/store_{serve,rotate,principal}_d_cx_platform.v files that stayed with it left under D73a: code exposes register_cli_verb and the store\'s own init() registers store-serve, store-health, store-rotate-kek and store-mint-principal into cmd\'s verb table. The row takes status=extracted the day ft\'s half leaves or is re-allocated']
  [repo name=cx-platform-db group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxdb pins='cx-core-code' status=extracted at=1834c802b4da2c4e6cba362ceb790f46b392157d about='external database access: $sql-*, $redis-*, the drivers' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), a V product: the RS-24 vcx/cxdb/ split (module cxdb) already stood alone from vcx/platform/, so extraction moved it out whole -- the sql, redis and db rows of registry/modules.cxd now name their spec, corpus and code under deps/cx-platform-db/, and xap (its only in-tree consumer, per its own pins=) reaches the dispatch registration through the pin, not a tracked path. It has no [path] rules any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records']
  [repo name=cx-platform-fabric group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=fabric pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-identity cx-platform-net' status=extracted at=6e455f86eeaaa6e6451319fc35884ac22c67978d about='messaging and fabric-serve' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, D73a; #1591 item K3): its V module vcx/fabric/ (module fabric) compiles from deps/cx-platform-fabric/vcx through -path and its spec, corpus and source are graded from the pin. vcx/cmd/fabric_serve_d_cx_platform.v left through the CLI-verb-registry hook D73a already gives cx-platform-store: code exposes register_cli_verb and fabric\'s own init() registers fabric-serve into cmd\'s verb table. NOT YET PUSHED to cx-home/cx-platform-fabric (component-repo pushes are the integrator\'s, RS-8; the commit is prepared in the mover\'s clone and named by sha in RESULTS.md, per the K3 brief). It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records']
  [repo name=cx-platform-xap group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=xap pins='cx-platform-net cx-platform-mail cx-platform-identity cx-platform-store cx-platform-db cx-platform-fabric' about='the application host, compose, dist, schema, market, the reference deployments']
  [repo name=cx-platform-flow group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=2ed490d6ab328cad54071a46b2d1dbc4231144aa about='workflow; its CLI verbs stay in the binary' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-20, #1591 item 15), the second of them. Its [path] rules are retired because it owns no tracked path here any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records. What RS-20 kept in `cx` is claimed by rules of its own and not by this row: the `cx flow` verbs (vcx/cmd/flow*.v, repo=cx) and the flow-perform act seam (vcx/platform/coordination.v, repo=cx-platform-xap)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-connector group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=5d4bebe7fc0d00b18e8b69fa8c257afa89ff834c about='the connector kit and sync' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, RS-27; #1591 item K3), a pure-CX package (RS-25: connector\'s twelfth native builtin retired with the mock\'s own declaration, so code=none). stdlib/connector.cx, spec/03-approved/platform/{connector,sync}.md, conformance/platform/{connector,sync}.cxd and reference/connectors/ leave whole; registry/modules.cxd\'s connector and sync rows now name deps/cx-platform-connector/ directly. The two real-socket lane V test files (vcx/tests/connector_live_test.v, connector_webhook_test.v) leave too, byte-identical, into the pinned repository\'s own vcx/tests/ -- but a ships=package repo carries no V toolchain of its own (RS-25), so the LANE MOVED AND THE STEP DID NOT, the test-sso-interop-lane shape (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 11): make target test-connector-real-lanes runs them out of deps/cx-platform-connector/vcx/tests/, against THIS tree\'s binary. It has no [path] rules any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records']
  [repo name=cx-platform-sso group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=1e814e5aae6327a8218cc3fe69b43a03517e92bf about='enterprise sign-on, the interop lane' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 11), the first of them. It has no [path] rules because it owns no tracked path here any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records, and the gate exempts a status=extracted repo from the empty-repo refusal for exactly that reason -- the row is the pin\'s counterpart, not a plan waiting to be executed']
  [repo name=cx-platform-ux group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=ef9248093389d42f6726042bfc254351445db4bc about='the web and terminal surfaces' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 12), with cx-platform-agent: the x/ graduation. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s ux, ux-web and ux-tui rows name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-platform-agent group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=df505787c2498100ded95e45031fa2f9192b2d09 about='tools, mcp, mcp-server, a2a, a2a-xap, llm, run, adjudicate' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 12), with cx-platform-ux: the x/ graduation. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s eight agent rows name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-binding-python group=binding ring=none ships=pypi status=extracted about='cxlib for Python' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), one of the four active bindings left whole on one branch. It owns no tracked path here any more and there is no deps.cxd row — cx does not consume a binding — so, unlike a pinned repo, this row carries no at=: nothing here names a sha to check it against. cx-home/cx-binding-python carries a catch-up commit (named by sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xbindings/RESULTS.md) bringing its files to this branch\'s head byte-for-byte and re-pinning its own deps.cxd cx-private row to that head; the commit is not pushed (RS-8: a mover prepares, the integrator pushes)']
  [repo name=cx-binding-go group=binding ring=none ships=go-module status=extracted about='cxlib for Go' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), with cx-binding-python/-rust/-v. It owns no tracked path here any more and there is no deps.cxd row — cx does not consume a binding. cx-home/cx-binding-go carries a catch-up commit (sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xbindings/RESULTS.md) to this branch\'s head, its own deps.cxd re-pinned; not pushed (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-binding-rust group=binding ring=none ships=crate status=extracted about='cxlib for Rust' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), with cx-binding-python/-go/-v. It owns no tracked path here any more and there is no deps.cxd row — cx does not consume a binding. cx-home/cx-binding-rust carries a catch-up commit (sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xbindings/RESULTS.md) to this branch\'s head, its own deps.cxd re-pinned; not pushed (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-binding-v group=binding ring=none ships=v-module status=extracted about='the native reference binding' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), with cx-binding-python/-go/-rust: the superseded lang/_archived/v-cffi/ FFI approach leaves with it (its history rode with the V binding). It owns no tracked path here any more and there is no deps.cxd row — cx does not consume a binding. cx-home/cx-binding-v carries a catch-up commit (sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xbindings/RESULTS.md) to this branch\'s head, its own deps.cxd re-pinned; not pushed (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-binding-typescript group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-java group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-kotlin group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-csharp group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-swift group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-ruby group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-registry group=ecosystem ring=none ships=none about='the package index: the store, publisher keys, the publish program']
  [repo name=cx-decisions group=ecosystem ring=none ships=none about='the ledger, the process specs, the standing rules, design texts']
  [repo name=cx-tooling group=ecosystem ring=none ships=editor about='vscode, neovim, tree-sitter, completions, syntax, the installer, diagram']

  [; ── what the data format's extraction could not release (RULED: D68a): cx-core-data is
     status=extracted and owns no path here; these rules re-allocate the files it was
     allotted but that grade, build or document this tree, each with its reason ── ]
  [path prefix='third_party/re2' repo=cx why='the re2 submodule: the front door builds the archive cx-core-data\'s regex module links (-d cx_re2_lib_dir / cx_re2_static), beside the V fork pin it keeps (RULED: D68a)']
  [path exact='include/cx.h' repo=cx-core-code why='libcx\'s whole C ABI, sixteen code and platform declarations with the data ones; libcx is the language repository\'s artifact (RULED: D68a)']
  [path prefix='scripts/wasm/' repo=cx-core-code why='the wasm build compiles vcx/code (the evaluator) into libcx.wasm; it is a libcx build (RULED: D68a)']
