  [; ── RS-18 (owner D20a, #1591 item 12): a family's builtin REGISTRATION
       lives in `vcx/platform/<its dispatcher's basename>_register.v`, so
       every rule above places a register file with the dispatcher it
       registers WITHOUT a rule of its own — `stdlib_store_register.v` goes to
       cx-platform-store by the `stdlib_store` rule, and so on. Since RS-24
       (owner D28a, D32a) a SPLIT product's register files moved unchanged
       with their dispatchers into its `vcx/<vmodule>/` directory, where one
       directory rule places all of them — `stdlib_net_register.v` is net's by
       the `vcx/cxnet/` rule. That is the whole point of
       the naming rule and the answer to extract-db/REPORT.md's F-D1. xap's
       split moved `ring2_register.v` (the COMPOSER, which names no family)
       and `stdlib_xap_register.v` into `vcx/xap/`, where the directory rule
       below places them; flow's `coordination_register.v` keeps an `exact=`
       rule beside the seam's own (RS-20), for the reason that row states. Adding a rule per register
       file would be a dead rule the allocation gate refuses. ──────────── ]

